---The specifications for retries. Specifies one or more conditions for which this retry rule applies. Valid values are:
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRetryPolicy
---@field retryConditions? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList - connect-failure: Router will retry on failures connecting to Backend Services, for example due to connection timeouts. - refused-stream: Router will retry if the backend service resets the stream with a REFUSED_STREAM error code. This reset type indicates that it is safe to retry. - cancelled: Router will retry if the gRPC status code in the response header is set to cancelled - deadline-exceeded: Router will retry if the gRPC status code in the response header is set to deadline-exceeded - resource-exhausted: Router will retry if the gRPC status code in the response header is set to resource-exhausted - unavailable: Router will retry if the gRPC status code in the response header is set to unavailable
---@field numRetries? number Specifies the allowed number of retries. This number must be > 0. If not specified, default to 1.

---Specifies how to route matched traffic.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteAction
---@field timeout? string Optional. Specifies the timeout for selected route. Timeout is computed from the time the request has been fully processed (i.e. end of stream) up until the response has been completely processed. Timeout includes all retries.
---@field faultInjectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteFaultInjectionPolicy Optional. The specification for fault injection introduced into traffic to test the resiliency of clients to destination service failure. As part of fault injection, when clients send requests to a destination, delays can be introduced on a percentage of requests before sending those requests to the destination service. Similarly requests from clients can be aborted by for a percentage of requests. timeout and retry_policy will be ignored by clients that are configured with a fault_injection_policy
---@field idleTimeout? string Optional. Specifies the idle timeout for the selected route. The idle timeout is defined as the period in which there are no bytes sent or received on either the upstream or downstream connection. If not set, the default idle timeout is 1 hour. If set to 0s, the timeout will be disabled.
---@field retryPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRetryPolicy Optional. Specifies the retry policy associated with this route.
---@field destinations? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteDestinationList Optional. The destination services to which traffic should be forwarded. If multiple destinations are specified, traffic will be split between Backend Service(s) according to the weight field of these destinations.
---@field statefulSessionAffinity? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteStatefulSessionAffinityPolicy Optional. Specifies cookie-based stateful session affinity.

---Criteria for matching traffic. A RouteMatch will be considered to match when all supplied fields match.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteMatch
---@field method? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteMethodMatch Optional. A gRPC method to match against. If this field is empty or omitted, will match all methods.
---@field headers? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteHeaderMatchList Optional. Specifies a collection of headers to match.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteMatchList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteMatch[]

---Describes how to route traffic.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteRule
---@field matches? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteMatchList Optional. Matches define conditions used for matching the rule against incoming gRPC requests. Each match is independent, i.e. this rule will be matched if ANY one of the matches is satisfied. If no matches field is specified, this rule will unconditionally match traffic.
---@field action? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteAction Required. A detailed rule defining how to route traffic. This field is required.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteRuleList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteRouteRule[]

---The specification for cookie-based stateful session affinity where the date plane supplies a “session cookie” with the name "GSSA" which encodes a specific destination host and each request containing that cookie will be directed to that host as long as the destination host remains up and healthy. The gRPC proxyless mesh library or sidecar proxy will manage the session cookie but the client application code is responsible for copying the cookie from each RPC in the session to the next.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.GrpcRouteStatefulSessionAffinityPolicy
---@field cookieTtl? string Required. The cookie TTL value for the Set-Cookie header generated by the data plane. The lifetime of the cookie may be set to a value from 0 to 86400 seconds (24 hours) inclusive. Set this to 0s to use a session cookie and disable cookie expiration.

---HttpRoute is the resource defining how HTTP traffic should be routed by a Mesh or Gateway resource.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRoute
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was updated.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was created.
---@field meshes? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Meshes defines a list of meshes this HttpRoute is attached to, as one of the routing rules to route the requests served by the mesh. Each mesh reference should match the pattern: `projects/*/locations/*/meshes/` The attached Mesh should be of a type SIDECAR
---@field rules? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteRuleList Required. Rules that define how traffic is routed and handled. Rules will be matched sequentially based on the RouteMatch specified for the rule.
---@field description? string Optional. A free-text description of the resource. Max length 1024 characters.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the HttpRoute resource. It matches pattern `projects/*/locations/*/httpRoutes/http_route_name>`.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. Server-defined URL of this resource
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Set of label tags associated with the HttpRoute resource.
---@field gateways? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Optional. Gateways defines a list of gateways this HttpRoute is attached to, as one of the routing rules to route the requests served by the gateway. Each gateway reference should match the pattern: `projects/*/locations/*/gateways/`
---@field hostnames? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Required. Hostnames define a set of hosts that should match against the HTTP host header to select a HttpRoute to process the request. Hostname is the fully qualified domain name of a network host, as defined by RFC 1123 with the exception that: - IPs are not allowed. - A hostname may be prefixed with a wildcard label (`*.`). The wildcard label must appear by itself as the first label. Hostname can be "precise" which is a domain name without the terminating dot of a network host (e.g. `foo.example.com`) or "wildcard", which is a domain name prefixed with a single wildcard label (e.g. `*.example.com`). Note that as per RFC1035 and RFC1123, a label must consist of lower case alphanumeric characters or '-', and must start and end with an alphanumeric character. No other punctuation is allowed. The routes associated with a Mesh or Gateways must have unique hostnames. If you attempt to attach multiple routes with conflicting hostnames, the configuration will be rejected. For example, while it is acceptable for routes for the hostnames `*.foo.bar.com` and `*.bar.com` to be associated with the same Mesh (or Gateways under the same scope), it is not possible to associate two routes both with `*.bar.com` or both with `bar.com`.

---The Specification for allowing client side cross-origin requests.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteCorsPolicy
---@field maxAge? string Specifies how long result of a preflight request can be cached in seconds. This translates to the Access-Control-Max-Age header.
---@field exposeHeaders? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies the content for Access-Control-Expose-Headers header.
---@field allowHeaders? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies the content for Access-Control-Allow-Headers header.
---@field allowCredentials? boolean In response to a preflight request, setting this to true indicates that the actual request can include user credentials. This translates to the Access-Control-Allow-Credentials header. Default value is false.
---@field allowOrigins? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies the list of origins that will be allowed to do CORS requests. An origin is allowed if it matches either an item in allow_origins or an item in allow_origin_regexes.
---@field disabled? boolean If true, the CORS policy is disabled. The default value is false, which indicates that the CORS policy is in effect.
---@field allowMethods? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies the content for Access-Control-Allow-Methods header.
---@field allowOriginRegexes? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies the regular expression patterns that match allowed origins. For regular expression grammar, please see https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax.

---Specifications of a destination to which the request should be routed to.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteDestination
---@field requestHeaderModifier? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderModifier Optional. The specification for modifying the headers of a matching request prior to delivery of the request to the destination. If HeaderModifiers are set on both the Destination and the RouteAction, they will be merged. Conflicts between the two will not be resolved on the configuration.
---@field weight? number Specifies the proportion of requests forwarded to the backend referenced by the serviceName field. This is computed as: - weight/Sum(weights in this destination list). For non-zero values, there may be some epsilon from the exact proportion defined here depending on the precision an implementation supports. If only one serviceName is specified and it has a weight greater than 0, 100% of the traffic is forwarded to that backend. If weights are specified for any one service name, they need to be specified for all of them. If weights are unspecified for all services, then, traffic is distributed in equal proportions to all of them.
---@field serviceName? string The URL of a BackendService to route traffic to.
---@field responseHeaderModifier? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderModifier Optional. The specification for modifying the headers of a response prior to sending the response back to the client. If HeaderModifiers are set on both the Destination and the RouteAction, they will be merged. Conflicts between the two will not be resolved on the configuration.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteDestinationList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteDestination[]

---The specification for fault injection introduced into traffic to test the resiliency of clients to destination service failure. As part of fault injection, when clients send requests to a destination, delays can be introduced by client proxy on a percentage of requests before sending those requests to the destination service. Similarly requests can be aborted by client proxy for a percentage of requests.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicy
---@field delay? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicyDelay The specification for injecting delay to client requests.
---@field abort? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicyAbort The specification for aborting to client requests.

---Specification of how client requests are aborted as part of fault injection before being sent to a destination.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicyAbort
---@field httpStatus? number The HTTP status code used to abort the request. The value must be between 200 and 599 inclusive.
---@field percentage? number The percentage of traffic which will be aborted. The value must be between [0, 100]

---Specification of how client requests are delayed as part of fault injection before being sent to a destination.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicyDelay
---@field fixedDelay? string Specify a fixed delay before forwarding the request.
---@field percentage? number The percentage of traffic on which delay will be injected. The value must be between [0, 100]

---Specifies how to select a route rule based on HTTP request headers.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatch
---@field suffixMatch? string The value of the header must end with the contents of suffix_match.
---@field presentMatch? boolean A header with header_name must exist. The match takes place whether or not the header has a value.
---@field regexMatch? string The value of the header must match the regular expression specified in regex_match. For regular expression grammar, please see: https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax
---@field header? string The name of the HTTP header to match against.
---@field exactMatch? string The value of the header should match exactly the content of exact_match.
---@field invertMatch? boolean If specified, the match result will be inverted before checking. Default value is set to false.
---@field rangeMatch? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatchIntegerRange If specified, the rule will match if the request header value is within the range.
---@field prefixMatch? string The value of the header must start with the contents of prefix_match.

---Represents an integer value range.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatchIntegerRange
---@field start? number Start of the range (inclusive)
---@field ["end"]? number End of the range (exclusive)

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatchList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatch[]

---The specification for modifying HTTP header in HTTP request and HTTP response.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderModifier
---@field set? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringMap Completely overwrite/replace the headers with given map where key is the name of the header, value is the value of the header.
---@field add? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringMap Add the headers with given map where key is the name of the header, value is the value of the header.
---@field remove? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Remove headers (matching by header names) specified in the list.

---Static HTTP response object to be returned.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHttpDirectResponse
---@field bytesBody? string Optional. Response body as bytes. Maximum body size is 4096B.
---@field status? number Required. Status to return as part of HTTP Response. Must be a positive integer.
---@field stringBody? string Optional. Response body as a string. Maximum body length is 1024 characters.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRoute[]

---Specifications to match a query parameter in the request.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteQueryParameterMatch
---@field exactMatch? string The value of the query parameter must exactly match the contents of exact_match. Only one of exact_match, regex_match, or present_match must be set.
---@field queryParameter? string The name of the query parameter to match.
---@field regexMatch? string The value of the query parameter must match the regular expression specified by regex_match. For regular expression grammar, please see https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax Only one of exact_match, regex_match, or present_match must be set.
---@field presentMatch? boolean Specifies that the QueryParameterMatcher matches if request contains query parameter, irrespective of whether the parameter has a value or not. Only one of exact_match, regex_match, or present_match must be set.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteQueryParameterMatchList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteQueryParameterMatch[]

---The specification for redirecting traffic.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRedirect
---@field httpsRedirect? boolean If set to true, the URL scheme in the redirected request is set to https. If set to false, the URL scheme of the redirected request will remain the same as that of the request. The default is set to false.
---@field hostRedirect? string The host that will be used in the redirect response instead of the one that was supplied in the request.
---@field portRedirect? number The port that will be used in the redirected request instead of the one that was supplied in the request.
---@field responseCode? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRedirectResponseCodeEnum|string The HTTP Status code to use for the redirect.
---@field stripQuery? boolean if set to true, any accompanying query portion of the original URL is removed prior to redirecting the request. If set to false, the query portion of the original URL is retained. The default is set to false.
---@field pathRedirect? string The path that will be used in the redirect response instead of the one that was supplied in the request. path_redirect can not be supplied together with prefix_redirect. Supply one alone or neither. If neither is supplied, the path of the original request will be used for the redirect.
---@field prefixRewrite? string Indicates that during redirection, the matched prefix (or path) should be swapped with this value. This option allows URLs be dynamically created based on the request.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRedirectResponseCodeEnum "RESPONSE_CODE_UNSPECIFIED"|"MOVED_PERMANENTLY_DEFAULT"|"FOUND"|"SEE_OTHER"|"TEMPORARY_REDIRECT"|"PERMANENT_REDIRECT"

---Specifies the policy on how requests are shadowed to a separate mirrored destination service. The proxy does not wait for responses from the shadow service. Prior to sending traffic to the shadow service, the host/authority header is suffixed with -shadow. Mirroring is currently not supported for Cloud Run destinations.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRequestMirrorPolicy
---@field destination? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteDestination The destination the requests will be mirrored to. The weight of the destination will be ignored.
---@field mirrorPercent? number Optional. The percentage of requests to get mirrored to the desired destination.

---The specifications for retries.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRetryPolicy
---@field perTryTimeout? string Specifies a non-zero timeout per retry attempt.
---@field retryConditions? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Specifies one or more conditions when this retry policy applies. Valid values are: 5xx: Proxy will attempt a retry if the destination service responds with any 5xx response code, of if the destination service does not respond at all, example: disconnect, reset, read timeout, connection failure and refused streams. gateway-error: Similar to 5xx, but only applies to response codes 502, 503, 504. reset: Proxy will attempt a retry if the destination service does not respond at all (disconnect/reset/read timeout) connect-failure: Proxy will retry on failures connecting to destination for example due to connection timeouts. retriable-4xx: Proxy will retry fro retriable 4xx response codes. Currently the only retriable error supported is 409. refused-stream: Proxy will retry if the destination resets the stream with a REFUSED_STREAM error code. This reset type indicates that it is safe to retry.
---@field numRetries? number Specifies the allowed number of retries. This number must be > 0. If not specified, default to 1.

---The specifications for routing traffic and applying associated policies.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteAction
---@field urlRewrite? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteURLRewrite The specification for rewrite URL before forwarding requests to the destination.
---@field retryPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRetryPolicy Specifies the retry policy associated with this route.
---@field redirect? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRedirect If set, the request is directed as configured by this field.
---@field directResponse? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHttpDirectResponse Optional. Static HTTP Response object to be returned regardless of the request.
---@field timeout? string Specifies the timeout for selected route. Timeout is computed from the time the request has been fully processed (i.e. end of stream) up until the response has been completely processed. Timeout includes all retries.
---@field faultInjectionPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteFaultInjectionPolicy The specification for fault injection introduced into traffic to test the resiliency of clients to backend service failure. As part of fault injection, when clients send requests to a backend service, delays can be introduced on a percentage of requests before sending those requests to the backend service. Similarly requests from clients can be aborted for a percentage of requests. timeout and retry_policy will be ignored by clients that are configured with a fault_injection_policy
---@field idleTimeout? string Optional. Specifies the idle timeout for the selected route. The idle timeout is defined as the period in which there are no bytes sent or received on either the upstream or downstream connection. If not set, the default idle timeout is 1 hour. If set to 0s, the timeout will be disabled.
---@field destinations? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteDestinationList The destination to which traffic should be forwarded.
---@field corsPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteCorsPolicy The specification for allowing client side cross-origin requests.
---@field requestHeaderModifier? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderModifier The specification for modifying the headers of a matching request prior to delivery of the request to the destination. If HeaderModifiers are set on both the Destination and the RouteAction, they will be merged. Conflicts between the two will not be resolved on the configuration.
---@field responseHeaderModifier? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderModifier The specification for modifying the headers of a response prior to sending the response back to the client. If HeaderModifiers are set on both the Destination and the RouteAction, they will be merged. Conflicts between the two will not be resolved on the configuration.
---@field requestMirrorPolicy? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRequestMirrorPolicy Specifies the policy on how requests intended for the routes destination are shadowed to a separate mirrored destination. Proxy will not wait for the shadow destination to respond before returning the response. Prior to sending traffic to the shadow service, the host/authority header is suffixed with -shadow.
---@field statefulSessionAffinity? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteStatefulSessionAffinityPolicy Optional. Specifies cookie-based stateful session affinity.

---RouteMatch defines specifications used to match requests. If multiple match types are set, this RouteMatch will match if ALL type of matches are matched.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteMatch
---@field fullPathMatch? string The HTTP request path value should exactly match this value. Only one of full_path_match, prefix_match, or regex_match should be used.
---@field headers? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteHeaderMatchList Specifies a list of HTTP request headers to match against. ALL of the supplied headers must be matched.
---@field regexMatch? string The HTTP request path value must satisfy the regular expression specified by regex_match after removing any query parameters and anchor supplied with the original URL. For regular expression grammar, please see https://github.com/google/re2/wiki/Syntax Only one of full_path_match, prefix_match, or regex_match should be used.
---@field ignoreCase? boolean Specifies if prefix_match and full_path_match matches are case sensitive. The default value is false.
---@field prefixMatch? string The HTTP request path value must begin with specified prefix_match. prefix_match must begin with a /. Only one of full_path_match, prefix_match, or regex_match should be used.
---@field queryParameters? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteQueryParameterMatchList Specifies a list of query parameters to match against. ALL of the query parameters must be matched.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteMatchList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteMatch[]

---Specifies how to match traffic and how to route traffic when traffic is matched.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteRule
---@field matches? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteMatchList A list of matches define conditions used for matching the rule against incoming HTTP requests. Each match is independent, i.e. this rule will be matched if ANY one of the matches is satisfied. If no matches field is specified, this rule will unconditionally match traffic. If a default rule is desired to be configured, add a rule with no matches specified to the end of the rules list.
---@field action? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteAction The detailed rule defining how to route matched traffic.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteRuleList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteRouteRule[]

---The specification for cookie-based stateful session affinity where the date plane supplies a “session cookie” with the name "GSSA" which encodes a specific destination host and each request containing that cookie will be directed to that host as long as the destination host remains up and healthy. The gRPC proxyless mesh library or sidecar proxy will manage the session cookie but the client application code is responsible for copying the cookie from each RPC in the session to the next.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteStatefulSessionAffinityPolicy
---@field cookieTtl? string Required. The cookie TTL value for the Set-Cookie header generated by the data plane. The lifetime of the cookie may be set to a value from 0 to 86400 seconds (24 hours) inclusive. Set this to 0s to use a session cookie and disable cookie expiration.

---The specification for modifying the URL of the request, prior to forwarding the request to the destination.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.HttpRouteURLRewrite
---@field hostRewrite? string Prior to forwarding the request to the selected destination, the requests host header is replaced by this value.
---@field pathPrefixRewrite? string Prior to forwarding the request to the selected destination, the matching portion of the requests path is replaced by this value.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.IntegerList number[]

---`LbEdgeExtension` is a resource that lets the extension service influence the selection of backend services and Cloud CDN cache keys by modifying request headers.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbEdgeExtension
---@field labels? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringMap Optional. Set of labels associated with the `LbEdgeExtension` resource. The format must comply with [the requirements for labels](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/labeling-resources#requirements) for Google Cloud resources.
---@field forwardingRules? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Required. A list of references to the forwarding rules to which this service extension is attached. At least one forwarding rule is required. Only one `LbEdgeExtension` resource can be associated with a forwarding rule.
---@field extensionChains? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.ExtensionChainList Required. A set of ordered extension chains that contain the match conditions and extensions to execute. Match conditions for each extension chain are evaluated in sequence for a given request. The first extension chain that has a condition that matches the request is executed. Any subsequent extension chains do not execute. Limited to 5 extension chains per resource.
---@field name? string Required. Identifier. Name of the `LbEdgeExtension` resource in the following format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/lbEdgeExtensions/{lb_edge_extension}`.
---@field description? string Optional. A human-readable description of the resource.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was updated.
---@field loadBalancingScheme? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbEdgeExtensionLoadBalancingSchemeEnum Required. All forwarding rules referenced by this extension must share the same load balancing scheme. Supported values: `EXTERNAL_MANAGED`.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was created.

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbEdgeExtensionList gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbEdgeExtension[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbEdgeExtensionLoadBalancingSchemeEnum "LOAD_BALANCING_SCHEME_UNSPECIFIED"|"INTERNAL_MANAGED"|"EXTERNAL_MANAGED"

---`LbRouteExtension` is a resource that lets you control where traffic is routed to for a given request.
---@class gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbRouteExtension
---@field loadBalancingScheme? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.LbRouteExtensionLoadBalancingSchemeEnum Required. All backend services and forwarding rules referenced by this extension must share the same load balancing scheme. Supported values: `INTERNAL_MANAGED`, `EXTERNAL_MANAGED`. For more information, refer to [Backend services overview](https://cloud.google.com/load-balancing/docs/backend-service).
---@field forwardingRules? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.StringList Required. A list of references to the forwarding rules to which this service extension is attached. At least one forwarding rule is required. Only one `LbRouteExtension` resource can be associated with a forwarding rule.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was created.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the resource was updated.
---@field extensionChains? gcp.unstable.networkservices_v1beta1.ExtensionChainList Required. A set of ordered extension chains that contain the match conditions and extensions to execute. Match conditions for each extension chain are evaluated in sequence for a given request. The first extension chain that has a condition that matches the request is executed. Any subsequent extension chains do not execute. Limited to 5 extension chains per resource.
---@field name? string Required. Identifier. Name of the `LbRouteExtension` resource in the following format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/lbRouteExtensions/{lb_route_extension}`.
